saleforce_training Day-12

1. What is Salesforce DX?
  ->Salesforce DX (Developer Experience) is a modern development approach that enables source-driven development, team collaboration, version control integration, and automated deployment processes.
Salesforce DX helps developers:
* Manage source code efficiently
* Work collaboratively in teams
* Use version control systems like GitHub
* Automate deployments
* Improve development productivity
 Key Features
* Source-driven development
* Scratch orgs
* Salesforce CLI integration
* GitHub compatibility
* Continuous Integration (CI)

2. Why CLI Matters?
  ->The Salesforce Command Line Interface (CLI) allows developers to interact with Salesforce using terminal commands instead of only using the browser interface.
 Benefits of CLI
* Faster development
* Automation capabilities
* Easier deployments
* Better productivity
* Supports scripting
* Simplifies repetitive tasks
 Examples
* Create projects
* Authorize orgs
* Deploy metadata
* Run tests
* Retrieve source code
CLI tools are essential in modern enterprise development workflows.
3. Why GitHub Matters?
  ->GitHub is a version control platform that stores source code and tracks changes.
 Benefits of GitHub
* Tracks code history
* Enables team collaboration
* Supports code reviews
* Prevents accidental code loss
* Allows rollback to previous versions
* Facilitates deployment workflows
Without GitHub, managing large software projects becomes difficult and risky.
