 Revision Questions and Answers

 1. Why do enterprise teams use version control?
  ->Version control tracks code changes, enables collaboration, prevents code loss, and supports rollback when problems occur.
 2. Why is deployment workflow important?
  ->Deployment workflows ensure controlled releases, reduce risks, improve quality, and maintain consistency across environments.
3. What problems happen without collaboration tools?
  ->Teams may experience code conflicts, lost work, communication issues, duplication of effort, and deployment problems.
4. Why is Salesforce DX important?
  ->Salesforce DX supports source-driven development, team collaboration, automation, and modern development practices.
5. Why do developers prefer CLI tools?
  ->CLI tools are faster, support automation, improve productivity, and simplify repetitive development tasks.
6. Why do enterprise systems require rollback capability?
  ->Rollback allows organizations to quickly restore previous stable versions if deployment issues occur.
 7. Why should teams separate development and production?
  ->Separation prevents accidental production changes and allows safe testing before release.
 8. Why is source-driven development useful?
   ->Source-driven development improves version control, collaboration, deployment consistency, and project maintainability.
 9. Why is collaboration difficult in large projects?
   -> teams work on many features simultaneously, creating challenges related to communication, coordination, code conflicts, and deployment management.
 10. Why is engineering workflow important?
  ->Engineering workflows improve software quality, reliability, collaboration, scalability, testing, and deployment efficiency.

